@startuml
title ASM System Architecture (Dockerized with Celery, FastAPI, Postgres)

' Components
actor User as "User (API Client)"

cloud "Docker Environment" {
  node "FastAPI App" as api {
    [main.py] as apimain
    [endpoints.py] as apiend
    [init_db.py] as initdb
    [database.py] as dbconn
    [models.py] as dbmodels
    [schemas.py] as dbschemas
  }

  node "Celery Worker" as worker {
    [tasks.py] as tasks
    [celery_app.py] as celapp
  }

  node "Celery Beat" as beat {
    [celery_app.py] as celappbeat
  }

  database "Postgres DB" as pgdb {
    [ASM Schema] as asmschema
  }

  queue "Redis (Broker)" as redis

  folder "apis/" as apis {
    [dns.py]
    [shodan.py]
    [fofa.py]
    [pentest_tools.py]
    [crt_sh.py]
    [securitytrails.py]
    [ssllabs.py]
    [whois.py]
  }

  folder "processors/" as processors {
    [subdomain_processor.py]
    [mx_processor.py]
  }

  folder "utils/" as utils {
    [logging_utils.py]
    [validators.py]
    [formatters.py]
  }

  folder "output/" as output {
    [exporter.py]
  }

  folder "migrations/" as migrations {
    [Alembic Files]
  }
}

' Flows
User --> api : API Calls (e.g., /scans/instant)
api --> pgdb : SQLAlchemy Queries/Inserts
api --> redis : Trigger Celery Tasks (e.g., scan_domain_task)
redis --> worker : Queue Tasks
worker --> pgdb : Store Scan Data
worker --> apis : Call APIs (dns, shodan, etc.)
worker --> apis : Query crt.sh, Pentest-Tools, FOFA, SecurityTrails, Shodan
worker --> processors : Process Records
worker --> utils : Validation/Formatting
worker --> output : Generate Files (on API request)
beat --> redis : Schedule Tasks (daily/weekly/monthly)
initdb --> migrations : Run Alembic on Startup
migrations --> pgdb : Create/Update Schema

' Notes
note left of User
  APIs:
  - POST /subscriptions/add {domain, frequency}
  - POST /scans/instant {domain}
  - GET /scans/status/{scan_id}
  - DELETE /scans/terminate/{scan_id}
  - GET /scans/result/{scan_id}/json
  - GET /scans/result/{scan_id}/csv or /xlsx
end note

note right of pgdb
  Tables: domains, scans, subdomain_data
  Relationships: domains (1:N) scans (1:N) subdomain_data
end note

note right of worker
  Tasks: scan_domain_task (core scanning)
  check_scheduled_scans (queue pending subscriptions)
  Prioritization: Instant scans are flagged `priority` and run before other pending scans.
  Concurrency: Controlled by `MAX_CONCURRENT_SCANS` env.
end note

note bottom of beat
  Schedules: Daily / Weekly (Mon 00:00) / Monthly (1st 00:00) via Celery Beat
  Beat enqueues subscription scans in ascending domain_id order; priority scans are inserted ahead of pending non-priority scans.
end note

@enduml